.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt SETFACL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm setfacl
.Nd set or remove a POSIX access control list
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Fl s Ar acl_text
.Ar file ...
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Fl b
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
replaces the selected ACL on each
.Ar file .
By default the access ACL is selected.
.Fl d
selects the directory default ACL.
.Fl s
takes a complete ACL in the text syntax printed by
.Xr getfacl 1 ,
for example
.Dq user::rwx\ngroup::r-x\nother::--- .
.Fl b
removes the selected ACL; when no access ACL is stored, file mode bits
continue to provide the access permissions.
.Pp
Default ACLs can only be installed on directories.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getfacl 1 ,
.Xr chmod 1
